-- erwartet: M104
-- **«B3», paper cut 4 of five -- CLOSED by the breiter-Kontext rule
-- (SPRACHE-EFFIZIENZ #18).** `u32 + u32` with a `u64` return type.
--
-- The reader read *"`u32 + u32` leaves the width of the result type"*, concluded that the
-- RESULT TYPE was too small, widened it to `u64` -- **and got the identical refusal back.**
-- That was the finding-18 shape, and the refusal was correct then: the checker
-- added in the operands' width, so only the handwritten widening helped.
--
-- Since the breiter-Kontext rule the same shape computes in the declared `u64`
-- and stays silent; the `M104` this file pinned now fires only where the target
-- is not wider (same operands, same hint: `gift/1409`). The first line stays
-- frozen as the verdict before the rule; the `jedes_gift`-harness asserts the
-- other side for this file (no error at all), exactly like lane 191's E001 flips.
--
-- *A message that names the fault without naming the line it lives on sends the reader to
-- the wrong line*, and here it cost a whole attempt. The three shapes that DO work are in
-- `TUTORIAL.md` and in the note under this refusal.
module gift583 {

pub fn sum(a : u32, b : u32) -> u64
    effects { pure }
    costs <= 4 ops
{
    return a + b;
}

}
